     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi again,<div><br></div><div>Hope everyone is staying healthy! <br><br>I&#39;ve been reading the vignette on assigning diagnosis to different tissues as well as a previous question that was posted that was called &quot;Supervised Analysis&quot; back in 2015.<br><br>I&#39;m still unsure though of how to label a class/my ROI&#39;s to further utilize it in my analysis. I&#39;ve seen that the select function has been used primarily with specific <i>m/z</i> but I can&#39;t say that I know for certain a <i>m/z</i> within the data that could be used. <br><br>Please let me know if I can provide any addition details and  thanks for any help or input!<br><br>Emily</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "SkuuQcVYAgAJ",
   "from": "kbemis",
   "author": "6033d3c0e7d242fa",
   "date": "2020-04-22T01:49:50Z",
   "subject": "Re: Question Regarding How to Label Disease States",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Until effective coregistration with optical images is implemented, the only way to select an ROI is from an ion image using <font face=\"courier new, monospace\">selectROI()</font><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">.</font><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">This takes the same arguments as the </font><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">image()</font><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"> method, and returns a logical vector giving the indices of the selected region.</font></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">It is up to you to find an appropriate ion image to use, based either on data exploration or known m/z values that correlate with the region of interest. Unfortunately, I can&#39;t really help with that part.</font></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">-Kylie</font></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
