     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Kylie,<div><br></div><div>I was able to create ROI&#39;s but I am unsure of how to label them as injury versus normal. <br><br>I had seen previously you had mentioned to utilize &quot;<span style=\"font-family:monospace;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(0,0,0)\">diagnosis </span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(0,0,136)\">as</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(102,102,0)\">.</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(0,0,0)\">character</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(0,0,0)\">rep</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(0,0,0)\">NA</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> ncol</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(0,0,0)\">mydata</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)))&quot; </span><span style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><font color=\"#000000\">calling select before this didn&#39;t prompt the creation of an ROI so I&#39;m assuming this is where the code would change to selectROI from what had been posted so many releases ago. Then once that was completed I could utilize the lines that had followed to create the labels.<br><br>Thank you again for taking the time to help me get used to the software.</font></font></span></div><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></font></span></div><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><font color=\"#000000\">Emily<br></font></font></span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(102,102,0)\"><br><br><br><br></span></div></div>"
    ]
